Thanksgiving is tomorrow and may be an American holiday, but have you always wanted to add an Irish twist to your meal?&nbsp;&nbsp;
Here is your chance.&nbsp; We have a traditional potato dish called, colcannon, with the whole family will love.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Colcannon potatoes are Irish mashed potatoes with mixed greens of cabbage or kale and scallions.&nbsp;&nbsp;
PREP TIME=10 minutes
COOK TIME=25 minutes
TOTAL TIME=35 minutes
SERVINGS=4
Ingredients

4 Russet Potatoes (2 to 2 1/2 pounds), peeled and cut into large chunks.
Salt.
4-6 tablespoons of unsalted butter, plus more for serving.
3 lightly packed cups of cabbage, chard, kale, or other leafy green.
3 green onions, minced (About 1/2 cup).
1 cup cream or milk.&nbsp;

Directions

Boil the potatoes in a medium pot and cover with cold water by at least an inch.&nbsp; Add 2 tablespoons of salt and bring to a boil.&nbsp; Boil until the potatoes are fork tender-15-20 minutes.&nbsp; Drain in a colander.
Return the pot to the stove and set over medium-high heat.&nbsp; Melt the butter in the pot and once it is hot, add the greens.&nbsp; Cook the greens for 3-4 minutes or until they are wilted and have given off some of their water.&nbsp; Add the green onions and cook 1 minute more.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Pour in the cream or milk, mix well, and add the potatoes.&nbsp; Reduce the heat to medium.&nbsp; Use a fork or potato masher and mash the potatoes, mixing them up with the greens.&nbsp;
Add salt and a dollop of butter to taste.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Enjoy!
